          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A 22-year-old woman presents with her third episode of uncomplicated cystitis in</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A 22-year-old woman presents with her third episode of uncomplicated cystitis in six months. She is otherwise healthy and non-pregnant. Which of the following preventive measures is most appropriate to recommend first?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Long-term prophylactic ciprofloxacin for six months</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Fluoroquinolones are not recommended as first-line prophylaxis for recurrent uncomplicated UTIs due to increasing resistance (particularly fluoroquinolone-resistant E. coli in India) and adverse effects. Behavioural measures should be tried first.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Placement of an indwelling catheter to ensure regular bladder drainage</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Catheterisation increases UTI risk through biofilm formation and direct introduction of bacteria into the urinary tract. It is never indicated for prevention of recurrent uncomplicated UTIs.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Adequate fluid intake, complete bladder emptying, and post-coital voiding</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct! Behavioural measures — adequate hydration, avoiding urinary retention, and voiding after intercourse — are first-line preventive strategies for recurrent uncomplicated UTIs and carry no risk of antimicrobial resistance.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Monthly surveillance urine cultures regardless of symptoms</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Routine surveillance cultures in asymptomatic patients are not recommended for uncomplicated recurrent UTIs. Screening for asymptomatic bacteriuria is indicated only in specific populations such as pregnant women.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review UTI prevention strategies. Behavioural measures (adequate hydration, complete voiding, post-coital voiding) are recommended as the first-line approach before considering antibiotic prophylaxis."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done! Behavioural modifications are the safest and most appropriate first-line approach for preventing recurrent uncomplicated UTIs."
                }
              ],
